  text: " <i>CONTEXTUAL SUB-ENTRY CREATED</i> /\r\n=============================/ 
    \n<i>[RELATED UPLOADS WILL BE STORED AT THIS ENTRY]</i>\n\r\nPaved way back in
    the 40s over the deserted land of Wankchester, <link>Road 54</link> starts at
    the end of Road 53.9. This stretch of gravel sees little to no traffic whatsoever
    as the surrounding populace tends to keep to themselves______\n----------------------------------------------
    \n               /<i>CONTEXTUAL EDIT</i>/\n----------------------------------------------    
    \n  \n_At exactly 331 Km, and not a millimeter further, Road 54 features its
    only <u>Petro Station</u>. The thing is, and I kid you not: it is placed exactly
    at kilometer 331. This incredible feat of accuracy was commended by the unknown
    architect group, consisting of two friends. His brother remains unimpressed.\n----------------------------------------------\n              
    /<i>CONTEXTUAL EDIT</i>/\n----------------------------------------------    
    \n\n<link>Road 54</link>, as many a thing in life, finally ends at a cardinal
    crossroads that directs its travelers to its 3 nearest towns: \n\n                                   
    The <u>southern Mermot Ales</u>, the <u>western Whoopla Town</u>, and the <u>northern
    HiKen Biken</u>.\n\nThe crash of an undisclosed <u>VTT</u> on Oct 30th is currently
    known as an Event (REDACTED). "
